    Lay out the panel stack and its affine recombination
    
    The layer relation reduces its panels together: the new module assigns every panel its width and aligned offset, largest panel first; computes the equality factors of the stack challenge ranges with the low-bit pairing of the reference form; and builds the verifier's affine recombination of the panels' operand values, folding the batch coefficient, the call factor and the row weights, with the shown weight terms for weight panels. Focused tests cover the layout order, the equality ranges and the coefficient of one panel entry.
    
    This is partial progress: the stack sumcheck's rounds and the row claims are the next step.

